//
// A GUARDED UNIT ARM DOES NOT COVER ITS VARIANT (`@FR-M-Total` crossed with `@FR-M-Unit`).
// M-Unit: `V` matches an enum value whose variant is the unit variant V.  M-Total: `total(V)`
// is true, but `total(pat if cond) = false` — "a GUARDED arm NEVER secures totality, whatever its
// pattern" — and on an enum subject "a variant counts as covered only by a TOTAL arm"; a variant
// left uncovered with no `_` is a static error naming it.  Here the only arm for `Red` is
// guarded, every other variant has a bare unit arm, and there is no `_`.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: match on MtC is not exhaustive — missing: Red
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fires on 18594597b, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the missing variant.
// HOLDS: `unit-arms-cover-an-enum-without-a-wildcard` beside it.

enum MtC { Red, Green, Blue }

fn mt_f(c: MtC, x: integer) -> integer {
  match c {
    Red if x > 0 => 1,
    Green => 2,
    Blue => 3
  }
}

fn main() {
  assert(mt_f(MtC.Green, 1) == 2, "unreachable");
}
